35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I see a significant shift in technical staffing, with phenotyping technicians moving to industry and an influx of applicants for modelling and code posts. Additionally, senior modelling analysts are seconded abroad until next autumn, while the glasshouse crew remains intact.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I noticed that travel and bench-fee lines in the ledgers have been frozen for three seasons, but shipping charges have increased. The ministry has extended its bench-fee subsidy for glasshouse space, which is a positive development. Additionally, the renewed national computing agreement covers simulation and modelling hours at no charge, but animal-unit day rates have risen sharply due to last year's vivarium rebuild.","{""words"":63,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found that the shared spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks last year due to a lapsed service contract, and now one engineer covers three institutes. Additionally, three of the five partner field sites lost a whole season to flooding or fire, while indoor holding rooms remained uninterrupted.","{""words"":49,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I see that awards built on live breeding colonies overran schedule twice as often as those whose main risk sat in computation rather than biology. Additionally, the animal facility cleared its accreditation renewal in spring and gained resident veterinary cover, while glasshouse blocks are booked solid through two more growing cycles.","{""words"":51,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I see that catalogue-style awards continue to draw outside users a decade on, while several mechanism-focused ones ended with their central question unresolved. Additionally, the national repository deposit turnaround has improved significantly, with deposits now clearing review inside a few weeks.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, the bench-fee subsidy for glasshouse space is good news. I'm glad to hear that the glasshouse crew came through the restructuring at full strength, which aligns with the subsidy.

@Kenji, the shared spectroscopy suite's downtime is concerning. It's important to ensure that such critical instruments are well-maintained and have proper service contracts in place.

@Benjamin, the schedule overruns for awards built on live breeding colonies are notable. It might be worth considering the risks associated with such colonies when evaluating proposals.

@Toshio, the improved national repository deposit turnaround is a positive development. Efficient data deposition is crucial for the visibility and progress of research.","{""words"":105,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Kenji"",""Benjamin"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
